                    <h3>Your people, understood</h3>
                    <p>A living page for everyone who matters to you. What they need, how you connect, and where things get tangled.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

{# The Story — How It Works #}
<section class="story-section" id="how-it-works">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
        <div class="section-header">
            <h2 class="reveal">How the magic works</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="story-scene reveal">
            <div class="story-illustration">
                <img src="/assets/scene-1-late-night-chat.jpg" alt="Late night chat with Julie">
            </div>
            <div class="story-text">
                <h3>One night, you open the app.</h3>
                <p>Something's been on your mind — maybe your sister's been distant, or a friendship feels off, or you just need to think out loud. You tell Julie. She asks the kind of questions a good friend would ask, if that friend had perfect memory and zero judgment.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="story-scene reverse reveal">
            <div class="story-illustration">
                <img src="/assets/scene-2-out-in-the-world.jpg" alt="Out in the world, Julie works behind the scenes">
            </div>
            <div class="story-text">
                <h3>The next day, you show up differently.</h3>
                <p>You're at brunch with your sister. You listen a little closer. You try something new. Meanwhile, Julie is quietly working in the background — turning last night's conversation into little cards of understanding.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="story-scene reveal">
            <div class="story-illustration">
                <img src="/assets/scene-3-insights-appear.jpg" alt="New insights appear on the page">
            </div>
            <div class="story-text">
                <h3>You open the app again. Something new is there.</h3>
                <p>Your sister's page has a new insight: <em>"She pulls away when she feels judged."</em> Another one says: <em>"You two connect best when it's just the two of you."</em> You didn't tell Julie that. She just... noticed.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="story-scene reverse reveal">
            <div class="story-illustration">
                <img src="/assets/scene-4-deeper-conversation.jpg" alt="A deeper conversation with Julie">
            </div>
            <div class="story-text">
                <h3>And the next conversation goes deeper.</h3>
                <p>You ask Julie how to bring something up without making your sister shut down. Julie doesn't give you a script — she gives you something better. An understanding of what your sister actually needs to hear, based on everything she knows about both of you.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <p class="story-epilogue reveal">And so it goes. You talk, you live, Julie learns.<br>The pages get richer. The advice gets sharper.<br>The people in your life start to feel a little closer.</p>
    </div>
</section>

